# TODO - Versioned host-capability call ABI

## Objective

Generalize the semantic capability-ID pattern proven by the DOOM corpus into the
VM ABI. Keep capability identity separate from transport: define versioning,
argument/result types, pointer/range validation, blocking rules, failure
semantics, capability discovery, and a deterministic call-frame representation
without requiring a literal new Malbolge opcode. Interpreters, JITs, and AOT
runners may lower the same call frame differently, but guest-visible behavior
and
validation must agree. The DOOM source ABI currently exercises version-1
external-effect categories spanning guest-memory provisioning, diagnostics/exit,
video/input, PCM audio, raw file I/O, UDP transport, and monotonic time; those
application-local capabilities are design evidence, not yet the generic VM ABI.

## Acceptance

- One versioned semantic capability registry and deterministic call-frame format
  define capability identity independently from transport/backend selection.
- Argument/result widths, byte order, guest pointers/ranges, discovery,
  blocking/partial-progress behavior, failures, and unsupported-version behavior
  are explicit and fail closed.
- Guest ranges are validated before host effects, and no host pointer, host libc
  calling convention, platform handle, or multimedia ABI leaks into guest state.
- Interpreter, JIT, AOT, and other admitted execution tiers pass the same
  capability vectors with equivalent guest-visible memory/results/diagnostics
  and
  effect ordering.
- The lowering contract does not require a new Malbolge opcode; any eventual
  encoding mechanism remains separate from semantic capability identity.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `runtime/`, `execution/`, `vm/`,
  `tools/tidy/`, and `tests/vm/`.
- Required evidence: canonical frame vectors, accepted/rejected range fixtures,
  discovery/version failures, host-error vectors, blocking/partial-progress
  fixtures, and cross-tier differential results.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `deterministic-c-to-malbolge-abi` and
  `canonical-malbolge-target-profile`.

**DOOM execution telemetry extension.**

Specify guest-directed relative-mouse capture and optional execution telemetry
as
versioned capabilities. Telemetry carries a language identifier, source
identity,
execution location, and active instruction text; C line reporting and Malbolge
cell/instruction reporting must use the same semantic record without influencing
guest behavior.

